{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1375,
 "dur": 45.809,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Mayor Primrose banned the ugly gray rocks under Tidyton's train tracks.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.544
  },
  {
   "text": "She planted a lawn instead. With tulips. And one garden gnome.",
   "s": 3.744,
   "e": 6.533
  },
  {
   "text": "It looked lovely, until the first rain turned the lawn into chocolate pudding.",
   "s": 6.733,
   "e": 10.117
  },
  {
   "text": "The wooden sleepers sank. The rails went wobbly, like cooked spaghetti.",
   "s": 10.317,
   "e": 13.344
  },
  {
   "text": "So the 8:15 train arrived bouncing like a rocking horse. At 11:40.",
   "s": 13.544,
   "e": 17.891
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the grass grew so tall the station master needed a ladder to spot the train.",
   "s": 18.091,
   "e": 21.902
  },
  {
   "text": "Her fix: mow the tracks every morning. A cow moved in and did it for free.",
   "s": 22.102,
   "e": 25.627
  },
  {
   "text": "By Friday, the train was stuck in the mud, and the cow was faster.",
   "s": 25.827,
   "e": 28.083
  },
  {
   "text": "So what were those ugly rocks doing all along?",
   "s": 28.283,
   "e": 30.109
  },
  {
   "text": "A train presses down like three hundred elephants. Sharp rocks lock together like puzzle pieces and hold the track still.",
   "s": 30.409,
   "e": 36.561
  },
  {
   "text": "And rain runs straight through the gaps. Grass holds water like a sponge.",
   "s": 36.761,
   "e": 40.17
  },
  {
   "text": "The rocks came back on Monday.",
   "s": 40.57,
   "e": 41.783
  },
  {
   "text": "Mayor Primrose painted them pink. The cow approved.",
   "s": 41.983,
   "e": 44.509
  }
 ],
